# ============================================================================
# THE HUMANS ARE FINE — production repository guard
#
# This repository is deployed verbatim by GitHub Pages. Anything committed here
# is publicly readable. Collector code, credentials, fixtures, editorial
# standards and internal reports must never be staged.
#
# Collector infrastructure lives at <workspace>/newsroom/fdw — outside this
# repository entirely. The rules below are the second line of defence for
# anything that gets copied in by accident.
# ============================================================================

# --- Internal working material (never published) ----------------------------
content/
docs/
fdw/
reports/
tests/
fixtures/
tmp/

# The collector lives outside this repository; this rule is the second line of
# defence if it is ever copied in. It must stay narrow: /newsroom/ is a PUBLIC
# page (Inside the AI Newsroom). A bare "newsroom/" rule silently excluded that
# page from the repository, so it could never have deployed. 2026-10-29.
newsroom/fdw/

# newsroom/ holds one public page and nothing else. Allow-list it rather than
# deny-list the collector subfolder: the isolation test proved that a new file at
# newsroom/probe-collector.ps1 was still stageable, i.e. any script dropped there
# would have been published by the next `git add -A`. 2026-10-30.
newsroom/*
!newsroom/index.html

# --- Credentials and environment -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
secrets*
credentials*

# --- Local scratch captures and probe output --------------------------------
# Root-level dumps produced while inspecting the live site. The deployed pages
# are the tracked *.html files; none of these belong in the archive.
/*.txt
/*.png
/*.json
/*.pdf
/*.csv
/*.log
/*.zip
# llms.txt is a PUBLIC discovery file, not a scratch capture. The /*.txt rule
# above silently excluded it, so the AI discovery resource could never deploy.
# Same failure mode as the newsroom/ rule: a broad deny-list hiding a public
# file that everything downstream assumed was shipping. 2026-11-01.
!/llms.txt
/live-*
/raw-*
/gh-index.html
/ghheaders.txt
/index
/landing.html
/page.html
/page3.html

# --- Shell/PowerShell mishap artefacts --------------------------------------
# Names that appear when a broken expansion is redirected to a file.
/$null
/System.Collections.Hashtable
/'

# --- Editor and OS noise ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# --- Internal editorial governance records (never published) ----------------
# approval-register.json and discovery-log.json were served publicly at
# /editorial/ because no rule covered this directory: the guard at the top of
# this file names "editorial standards" but only denied content/ docs/ fdw/
# reports/ tests/ fixtures/ tmp/. Published 2026-11-05, removed 2026-11-05.
# These records stay in git history; they are moved to the private vault, and
# the removal is forward-only on the tree. Never add a rule that re-includes them.
editorial/

# --- Internal build and verification tooling (never published) --------------
# All 44 .ps1 build/verification scripts, their two JSON state files and the
# git hook template were served publicly at /scripts/*.ps1 until 2026-11-06,
# because GitHub Pages deploys the root of `main` verbatim and no rule covered
# the directory. They now live outside the repository entirely:
#   Documents\StarNet-Outputs\thaf-tooling-archive-20261106
#
# This rule is the SECOND line of defence only. An ignore rule is a staging
# filter: it does not stop `git add -f`, and it cannot express intent. The
# first line of defence is publish-gate.ps1, which enumerates the tree Pages
# will actually serve and admits only paths on an explicit allow-list. It runs
# as a pre-commit hook and again against the ref before any push.
scripts/

# --- Never publish a script, record or key, wherever it is put ---------------
# Belt, braces and a third strap: if one of these is ever dropped outside the
# directories named above, the publish gate still refuses the tree.
*.ps1
*.psm1
*.psd1
*.json
*.env
*.log
